-- title:
--   Label exponents and operational slot extraction
-- statement:
--   Let $n,r\in\mathbb N$ and let $o_1,o_2$ be Boolean query functions on subsets of $[n]=\{0,\ldots,n-1\}$. Put $E=[n]\times\{0,1\}$, let paired states be subsets of $E$, and write $d(S)=n-\operatorname{pairedRank}(r,o_1,o_2,S)$ using truncated natural subtraction. A transversal has one label in each pair; a defect $(i,k)$ has empty pair $i$, full pair $k$, and one label elsewhere, with $i\ne k$. For any finite subset $A$ of any label type, define its squarefree exponent vector
--   $$\lambda_A=\sum_{e\in A}e_e.$$
--   Here $e_e$ is the unit exponent at $e$. For paired sets $B,R\subseteq E$, free-pair set $U\subseteq[n]$, distinguished index $t\in[n]$, and rational $q$, begin with the operational omitted-label polynomial
--   $$F_q(X)=\sum_{\substack{S\subseteq E\\|S|=n}}q^{d(S)}\prod_{e\in E\setminus S}X_e.$$
--   The operational slot polynomial is defined by the following fixed sequence. Differentiate once in every label of $E\setminus(B\cup R\cup(U\times\{0,1\}))$. Preserve labels in $R$ or pair $t$; identify the two labels at every other index of $U$ with its label-zero variable, and set other variables to zero. For every $s\in U\setminus\{t\}$, differentiate in $X_{(s,0)}$ and then set that variable to zero, extracting exponent exactly one. Finally substitute
--   $$X_e\longmapsto\sum_{\substack{h\in R\\h=e}}Y_h+\sum_{\substack{b\in\{0,1\}\\(t,b)=e}}Z_b.$$
--   The resulting rational polynomial is indexed by $R\sqcup\{0,1\}$. This definition uses the operational query-based weights; it assumes no exact-oracle or positivity conditions and does not itself prove that the result has degree two. The final substitution can split a label into two variables when the active sets overlap.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/OmittedTutteNormalization.lean#L18-L21

